#N canvas 0 0 1400 1100 10;
#X text 20 20 glow.pd: tilt-driven light toy for a greyscale/varibright 64 \, on mlrv-pd's serialosc.pd + grid.pd primitives. inlet 0: grid keys (list x y state) + direct tilt <x> <y> <z> / clear / tick. inlet 1: tilt sensor tuples (sensor x y z). creation arg \$1 = tick ms (required \, e.g. 60). outlet 0 = LED x y level. comet velocity integrates tilt deviation from a slow-adapting center (hold a tilt and it recenters) \, friction 0.94 \, wall bounce damped \, speed clamped +-2. phosphor table decays *0.82 per tick \, quantized int(level*1.0666) \, emit-on-change only (second table tracks shown levels). press = instant full-bright dot. shake (|dx|+|dy|+|dz| > 50) sets a clear flag consumed by the next loop. verified: tests/run_glow_test.sh.;
#X text 20 100 copies: BX/BY x2 (phys idx) \, VX/VY x3 (phys tilt flip) \, CX/CY x2 (devcold adapt) \, CZ x1 \, IH x6 (bright showncmp x y pkshidx clearidx) \, QH x3 (cmp shownwrite ledpack). loop: tick -> IDX:=0 -> [until] body x64 -> stop+phys+ballwrite+clear-reset. body: latch i -> clear? zero+quantize : decay+writeback+quantize -> compare vs shown -> emit LED + update shown.;
